1. When scanning codebase for context, do not look at files/folders that are not real code (unless specified in the prompt), such as: node_modules, .next, .git, .gitignore, .cert, .env, *.md files, package-lock.json, and similar non-code artifacts.

2. When needing to look for a skill, from root folder, look in the .agents/skills folder.

3. When being asked for code modification, only generate into output your modification and brief explanation. For each file that needs modification, only modify what needs modification and do not mess up other part that is not related.

4. When being asked to explain something, only generate the answer without modifying any code or running any command.

5. When a user requests a code modification that involves multiple layers of the stack, follow this workflow in order. Skip any step not required by the user prompt.

   ```
   Step 1:  Modify Frontend Layout
            Files: homepage/app/**, homepage/components/**, adminPage/app/**, adminPage/components/**
            (UI changes only — pages, components, styling)

   Step 2:  Update Frontend Types & API Hooks
            Files: adminPage/types/index.ts, adminPage/hooks/**, adminPage/store/**
            (Define or update TypeScript interfaces matching new data shapes)

   Step 3:  Update DB Schema
            Files: backend/prisma/schema.prisma, backend/prisma/schema.sqlserver.prisma
            (Add/modify Prisma models, run migrations)

   Step 3b: Migrate Existing Data
            (After schema migration, write and run a data migration script that preserves all existing rows.
             For new columns with defaults, use UPDATE statements to backfill old records.
             Never DROP/CREATE tables — use ALTER TABLE ADD columns with defaults so no data is lost.
             Verify row counts match before/after migration.)
            Files: backend/scripts/data-migrations/**
            (One-time migration scripts for transforming existing data into new schema shape)

   Step 4:  Update Backend DTOs
            Files: backend/src/db/dtos/**
            (Define data transfer objects that map between DB and API layer)

   Step 5:  Update Backend Business Logic & Services
            Files: backend/src/db/services/**
            (Implement CRUD logic, validation, transformations)

   Step 6:  Write Backend Tests (for modified services)
            Files: backend/src/**/*.test.ts, backend/src/**/*.spec.ts
            (Unit tests for services, integration tests for database queries)

   Step 7:  Update Backend API Routes & Schemas
            Files: backend/src/api/routes/**, backend/src/api/schemas/**
            (Define/update routes, request validation schemas, response types)

   Step 8:  Write Backend API Tests (for modified routes)
            Files: backend/src/api/**/*.test.ts, backend/src/tests/**
            (Integration tests for API endpoints — request/response, auth, error handling)

   Step 9:  Wire Frontend to API
            Files: adminPage/app/**/page.tsx, adminPage/app/**/*.tsx, homepage/lib/**
            (Connect frontend components to the updated API endpoints)

   Step 10: Write Frontend Tests (for modified components/pages)
            Files: adminPage/**/*.test.ts, adminPage/**/*.spec.ts,
                   homepage/**/*.test.ts, homepage/**/*.spec.ts
            (Component rendering, hook behavior, page smoke tests with mocked API)

   Step 11: Update Config Files
            Files: .env.local, docker/.env.docker, backend/.env, etc.
            (Environment variables, API URLs, feature flags)

   Step 12: Update Deployment Config
            Files: docker/*.Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, CI/CD configs
            (Docker, infrastructure, pipeline changes)
   ```

   Constraint: If a step is not required in the user prompt, skip it.
   Test steps (6, 8, 10) are only run when the user explicitly asks for testing (e.g., "add tests", "test it", "make sure it works") or when modifying critical business logic that could break existing functionality.